---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_ADDRESS } from '../consts';
---

<Base
	title="Privacy Policy — Brand in Progress"
	description="How Brand in Progress collects, uses, and protects your personal data."
>
	<main class="legal">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="kicker"><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="updated">Last updated: November 2026</p>

			<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
			<p>
				Brand in Progress ("we", "us") is a product sourcing and development company
				based at {CONTACT_ADDRESS}. You can reach us at
				<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
				We are the data controller for the personal data collected through this website.
			</p>

			<h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
			<p>When you contact us through this website (form or email), we collect:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your name</li>
				<li>Your email address</li>
				<li>The subject and content of your message</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We do not use advertising cookies, analytics trackers, or any form of
				profiling. The contact form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a
				privacy-friendly anti-spam check that does not track you across websites.
			</p>

			<h2>3. Why we collect it (legal basis)</h2>
			<p>
				We use your data solely to respond to your enquiry and, if you become a
				client, to prepare and perform our services. The legal basis is our
				legitimate interest in replying to business enquiries and, where applicable,
				pre-contractual steps at your request (Art. 6(1)(b) and 6(1)(f) GDPR).
			</p>

			<h2>4. Where your data is processed</h2>
			<p>Your message passes through the following service providers, strictly to deliver it to us:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (hosting & spam protection)</li>
				<li><strong>Resend</strong> (email delivery)</li>
				<li><strong>Google Sheets</strong> (our internal contact log)</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				These providers process data on our behalf and may be located outside the
				EU/EEA; transfers rely on their standard contractual safeguards. We never
				sell or share your data with anyone else.
			</p>

			<h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
			<p>
				Enquiry data is kept for up to 24 months, unless a business relationship
				requires longer retention or you ask us to delete it sooner.
			</p>

			<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				If you are in the EU/EEA, you have the right to access, correct, delete, or
				restrict the processing of your personal data, and to lodge a complaint with
				your local data protection authority. To exercise any of these rights, email
				us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> — we respond
				within 30 days.
			</p>

			<h2>7. Changes</h2>
			<p>
				We may update this policy from time to time. The current version is always
				published on this page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</Base>

<style>
	.legal {
		padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
	}
	.legal .wrap {
		max-width: 44rem;
	}
	h1 {
		font-size: 2.2rem;
		margin: 0.5rem 0 0.2rem;
	}
	.updated {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	h2 {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		margin: 1.8rem 0 0.5rem;
	}
	p,
	li {
		color: #3d3d3d;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}
	ul {
		padding-left: 1.3rem;
	}
	a {
		color: var(--ink);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--brand);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
</style>
